  "title": "Reasoning Economy Score (TES) and Adaptive Reasoning in AI",
  "summary": "This paper introduces the Token Economy Score (TES) to measure the accuracy gain of reasoning models across task types and deployment contexts, while exploring how adaptive reasoning mechanisms can optimize model efficiency. The results highlight the importance of task-specific reasoning strategies and deployment context in improving both performance and economics.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The TES metric measures the accuracy gain of reasoning models over non-reasoning baselines, normalized by generated-token multiplier.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Empirical analysis shows that task structure predicts reasoning efficiency better than nominal difficulty.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Results indicate that over-reasoning can lead to increased computational cost without proportional accuracy gains.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
